# Installed workspace CLI acceptance

The client source is the clean DEV-102 candidate 8f4dd72cb9c6c58c0860bb9125289986cfc180d1.
Control has its own installed source and binary identity. The two revisions may differ.
A client build revision must never be recorded as the installed Control revision.

Primary sources:
- The frozen DEL installed_acceptance_test.go exports installed-ready.json,
  installed-provenance.json, installed-control.bin, installation-ca.pem and admin-credential.
- The frozen DEL installed_scope_test.go exports person.json and scope-state.json.
- The installed administrator email comes from admin-credential.request.administrator_email.
- The workspace handler permits platform administrators to read every workspace in
  the installed tenant. A regular Portal member has narrower membership authority.
- https://pkg.go.dev/runtime/debug#BuildInfo documents Go build settings.
- https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/ssl.html documents certificate and hostname verification.
- https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/subprocess.html documents bounded child execution.
- https://docs.python.org/3.12/license.html provides the PSF licence.

Use the existing installation and public HTTPS operations. Create no database, server,
test account or second installation. Use the installer-issued credential and seeded
members. Preserve the real origins and certificate verification. The window owner joins
its existing network namespace and gives the CLI a private mount namespace with DNS
host entries for those exact origins. The host's hosts file remains unchanged.

Qualify CLI list/detail, bounded continuation, empty search, foreign-tenant refusal,
nonadministrator Admin login refusal, logout/replayed revoked session refusal and fresh
login recovery. A separate Portal HTTPS companion verifies an allowed member workspace
and refusal of a different workspace and tenant. Label those protocol checks separately
from the Admin-only CLI checks.

Reject missing inputs, a stale source/provenance pair, a binary hash mismatch, unsafe
credential files and incomplete scope relationships before a login. Do not skip a missing
case or turn an input refusal into an acceptance pass. Store only case names, stable
codes and request IDs; never store credential or raw HTTP/CLI output in the report.

The client uses the already-reviewed CLI dependencies (Cobra Apache-2.0, Go and x/sys
BSD-3-Clause and the existing YAML/terminal dependencies). The driver uses only the
Python 3.12 standard library under the PSF licence. Commercial and offline use and
redistribution are allowed under their notices. No model, dataset or dependency is added.

The installed endpoint is not ready yet. Harness validation is not installed acceptance.
